============================================================
          ODROID N2 DTB / DTBO UPDATED BUILD QUICK GUIDE
               I KEPT THE OLD TUTORIAL AT THE END
============================================================

1. INSTALL REQUIRED PACKAGES
----------------------------

sudo apt update

sudo apt install \
    git \
    make \
    device-tree-compiler \
    gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu \
    libssl-dev \
    bc \
    bison \
    flex \
    libncurses-dev


2. CONFIGURE THE BUILD ENVIRONMENT
----------------------------------

Edit ~/.bashrc :

nano ~/.bashrc

Add the following lines at the end of the file:

export ARCH=arm64
export CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu-

Apply the changes:

source ~/.bashrc

Verify:

echo $ARCH
echo $CROSS_COMPILE


3. VERIFY THE CROSS COMPILER
----------------------------

aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc -v


4. CLONE THE VOODIK KERNEL SOURCE
---------------------------------

git clone --depth 1 \
    -b lineage-22.1_odroidg12_64_1 \
    https://github.com/voodik/android_kernel_voodik_odroidg12.git

cd android_kernel_voodik_odroidg12


5. BUILD DTB / DTBO FILES
-------------------------

make dtbs


6. GENERATED OUTPUT FILES
-------------------------

arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/overlays/odroidn2/


7. VERIFY GENERATED OVERLAYS
----------------------------

ls -l arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/overlays/odroidn2/*.dtbo


8. REBUILD AFTER DTS MODIFICATIONS
----------------------------------

After modifying any .dts file:

make dtbs


NOTES
-----

- The legacy Linaro 7.4.1 toolchain was not required.
- Debian's gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu cross-compiler works correctly.
- PWM-related warnings may appear during compilation.
- These warnings do not prevent .dtbo files from being generated.

